                        "sense_id": "8db1bbb2-fc1b-337b-ab00-4f4292f2631c",
                        "entry_id": "f0731809-2b72-31c3-8ad0-5b4d3dd8da97",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vogel der Gattung Bergkrähen, gehört zur Familie der Raben und Krähen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "special"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9836ee05-2fb2-4004-8ee9-1e5956be8982",
                                "sense_id": "8db1bbb2-fc1b-337b-ab00-4f4292f2631c",
                                "text": "„Die Alpendohle lebt in den Bergen in Höhen von bis zu 6.000 m.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b85048b2-30a8-4a7b-ae45-4251cf767880",
                        "source_entry_id": "f0731809-2b72-31c3-8ad0-5b4d3dd8da97",
                        "source_sense_id": "8db1bbb2-fc1b-337b-ab00-4f4292f2631c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Vogel der Gattung Bergkrähen",
                        "target_lang_word": "alpine chough",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alpine chough",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e302f57-94ca-3c68-b607-91461d97f84d",
                                        "entry_id": "edb18b1f-a290-3251-9c45-7fa3a9a8b61b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A species of bird in the crow family (Corvidae) (Pyrrhocorax graculus), that breeds locally in the highest mountains of southern Europe, the Alps, across central Asia and India."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64c13f76-8a23-4350-857d-b630af182de2",
                                                "sense_id": "5e302f57-94ca-3c68-b607-91461d97f84d",
                                                "text": "In a sense these sections form refrains to the two couplets, in which two types of material are used: birdsong, consisting of the calls and cries of the alpine chough and the raven, and passages representing the flight of the alpine chough and the flight of the golden eagle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f137fe5-d009-4896-bf30-f4ad8be7a833",
                                                "sense_id": "5e302f57-94ca-3c68-b607-91461d97f84d",
                                                "text": "The alpine chough was seen by Edmund Hillary on his way to the summit of Mount Everest at 28,000 feet, and I believe it is likely that the little cache of biscuits and candy placed on the summit by Tensing Norkay in May, 1953, was visited by alpine choughs on their patrols in search of human debris."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3c59eec-ca3c-4396-bd77-0436277e4bfa",
                                                "sense_id": "5e302f57-94ca-3c68-b607-91461d97f84d",
                                                "text": "2002, Chough, entry in Maurice Burton, International Wildlife Encyclopedia, Volume 4: Chickaree - crabs, 3rd Edition, page 451,\nRed-billed and alpine choughs live in mountainous regions, but while the latter is strictly a montane species, the former also occurs at lower altitudes. In most countries where both species are found the alpine chough is more numerous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17af5d62-2b9b-44f4-9285-7af9f7c9a4bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "f0731809-2b72-31c3-8ad0-5b4d3dd8da97",
                        "source_sense_id": "8db1bbb2-fc1b-337b-ab00-4f4292f2631c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Vogel der Gattung Bergkrähen",
                        "target_lang_word": "chocard à bec jaune",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chocard à bec jaune",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bfdb004-84b0-31a3-82a5-a4cf4998b146",
                                        "entry_id": "5297f63b-50c5-33ab-9ff4-af6471ab517f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Espèce d'oiseau passereau des hautes montagnes d'Europe et d'Afrique du Nord, petit corvidé noir à bec jaune et pattes rouges."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f4ca085-ba71-4445-a618-48d63087c776",
                                                "sense_id": "9bfdb004-84b0-31a3-82a5-a4cf4998b146",
                                                "text": "Le chocard à bec jaune est un oiseau omnivore: insectes, œufs, invertébrés, graines et baies, charognes de rongeurs, … ... rien ne lui résiste, sans oublier les restes de repas des touristes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fec4289-12d9-4ed7-83a7-2d0b5917664f",
                                                "sense_id": "9bfdb004-84b0-31a3-82a5-a4cf4998b146",
                                                "text": "Habituellement, le Chocard à bec jaune peut nicher dans une caverne, sous un surplomb ou même dans une fissure d'une paroi rocheuse jusqu'à une altitude de 3500 m."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
